    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Education spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Education obligated $2.2B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Education recorded 652 awards with an average award size of $3.3M, and obligations fell 13.9% year over year. The FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Education buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Education buys a mix of financial services, IT services, research, and education support. The Department of Education obligated $939M for Other Activities Related to Credit Intermediation, $659M for Computer Systems Design Services, and $144M for Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities, among other categories."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Education's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of Education's largest contractors are primarily large IT and student-services firms. ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $340M, NELNET SERVICING LLC received $294M, and MAXIMUS EDUCATION LLC received $251M, with EDFINANCIAL SERVICES LLC at $198M and MAXIMUS FEDERAL SERVICES, INC. at $160M following behind."
